---
title: Paintings - Vintage Story Wiki
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "{{ lang }}/paintings/index.html"
---
{% import "macros/datatable.njk" as dt %}
{% import "macros/breadcrumb.njk" as bc %}
{{ bc.trail(lang, [{label: "Paintings"}]) }}
<h1>Paintings</h1>
<p class="muted">
  Purely decorative placed blocks with no recipe or drop table, so they don't appear anywhere else
  on this wiki &mdash; see the <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}info/">Info</a> page for why.
  {{ generated.paintings.length }} catalogued directly from the game's block definitions.
</p>
<p class="muted">Source: <code>blocktypes/wood/painting.json</code>. <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}sources/paintings/">Full details &rarr;</a></p>

{% call dt.datatable(60, "Search paintings...", ["Name", "Mod"]) %}
{% for item in generated.paintings | sort(false, false, "displayName") %}
  <tr data-search="{{ item.domain }}:{{ item.code }}" data-mod="{{ item.sourceMod }}" data-mod-label="{{ generated.mods | modName(item.sourceMod) }}"{{ dt.descriptionAttrs(item.description) }}>
    <td><a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}paintings/{{ item.domain }}/{{ item.code | slugify }}/">{{ item.displayName }}</a></td>
    <td><span class="tag">{{ item.sourceMod }}</span></td>
  </tr>
{% endfor %}
{% endcall %}

<h2 id="paintingtapestry-in-ruins-lookup">Which ruins contain a painting <span class="wip-badge">WIP</span></h2>
<p>
  Right now, each painting page (and every <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}items/">item/block</a> page) shows which
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}structures/">structures</a> it's found in, built from a flat pass over every schematic's block-code
  dictionary &mdash; it confirms the code is somewhere in that schematic, not where or how many times. <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tapestries/">Tapestries</a>
  already get a precise, per-instance version of this (decoded directly from each schematic's block-entity data); a proper lookup for paintings
  would need the same per-instance decoding, evaluated against <code>worldgen/storystructures.json</code> and <code>worldgen/structures.json</code> directly.
</p>
